{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And I also established, etc.</b> According to what we explained — that Elohim makes known to us that He distinguished between Himself and the fathers — His saying <b>and I also established</b> intends as though He said, 'And even though I established,' etc., or, 'And also that I established,' etc. — yet they did not attain to make known to them My name HaShem, as you have attained.'" "<b>Further,</b> it intends to say that this matter is something that HaShem blessed be He is obligated to do, as it were — besides that He revealed Himself to them by El Shaddai and promised them, He further established with them an oath, etc., and from now on He must fulfill His oath, and the matter is of necessity to be. And through this the hands of Moses will be strengthened when he knows that this matter has no impediment from being so. And even though He already answered him regarding what Moses had argued — that he should have delayed the mission until the time of the end — and He answered him and said to him <b>I am YHWH</b>, because He could not contain His compassion; still, there is reason to fear that Moses might slacken in completing the mission of the exodus when he sees all the stubbornness of Pharaoh's heart, or at the sea he might recoil backward. Therefore El Elyon made known to him that these matters are binding upon Him by the force of the oath to give them the land." "<b>et the land of their sojournings.</b> One must know why He was not satisfied with mentioning its name, ״אֶרֶץ כְּנָעַן״, and went back and said ״אֵת אֶרֶץ מְגוּרֵיהֶם״? Perhaps it intends to say that the sojourning had already begun from the days of the fathers, and the implication is to begin the count from the time of the fathers, as indeed it was. But it is still difficult, for He should have said ״אֶת אֶרֶץ כְּנַעַן אֶרֶץ מְגוּרֵיהֶם״ — why did He say ״אֵת״, which makes it appear as though they are two lands? Perhaps it intends to include the land of the Philistines, as I explained on the verse (Genesis 26:3) ״גּוּר בָּאָרֶץ הַזֹּאת, etc. כִּי לְךָ וּלְזַרְעֲךָ אֶתֵּן״, etc. — see there."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:03.707608150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}